<section class="subhero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">SimpleTen / Sacramento, California</div><h1 data-reveal="words">AI workflow automation for Sacramento businesses.</h1><p class="lede">Make the work between your tools more reliable. We build connected workflows that reduce retyping, organize follow-up, and give your team clearer handoffs.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="#contact">Discuss your workflow <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="button secondary" href="/#blueprint">How the blueprint works</a></div></div></section>
<section class="section light"><div class="wrap article-grid"><div class="article-copy"><h2 data-reveal="focus">Connect the steps that slow your team down.</h2><p>SimpleTen designs business automations around a defined process, using tools such as n8n where they fit. Predictable steps use clear rules; AI can help interpret or draft information when needed. We define the limits and human review points before a workflow goes live.</p><h3 id="lead-follow-up">Lead capture and follow-up</h3><p>Connect incoming inquiries from forms, email, and supported phone systems to the CRM. Organize contact details, route work to an owner, and prepare or trigger agreed follow-up steps. Where messages are sent automatically, the scope includes consent requirements, approved content, and escalation rules.</p><h3 id="operations">Operations and project handoffs</h3><p>Move an approved job into your project tools, create the agreed tasks, and keep status updates connected. We define what should happen when information is missing or a connection fails, so someone on your team can handle the exception instead of discovering it later.</p><h3 id="reporting">Reporting your team can use</h3><p>Bring selected data into a useful view of inquiries, appointments, project progress, or other agreed measures. We check how each number is defined and where it comes from. The aim is a consistent picture of the business, with clear owners for the underlying information.</p></div><aside class="scope-box"><h2>What we scope together</h2><ul><li>Documented triggers, steps, and owners</li><li>Connections to agreed business tools</li><li>Data mapping and permission review</li><li>Testing for normal and exception cases</li><li>Human review and escalation points</li><li>Handoff documentation and support options</li></ul><a class="button" href="#contact">Start with an assessment <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><small>Deliverables, timing, software costs, and ongoing support are agreed before a paid build begins.</small></aside></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap example-grid"><div class="example-copy"><span class="example-label">Example use case / illustrative</span><h2 data-reveal="words">A missed call still gets a next step.</h2><p>For a home-service team, a missed inquiry can turn into several manual tasks. An agreed follow-up workflow can put the inquiry in one place and make responsibility clear.</p></div><ol class="example-steps"><li>Receive a missed-call event from a supported phone system.</li><li>Match or create the contact in the CRM without duplicates.</li><li>Route the inquiry and prepare an approved follow-up step.</li><li>Record the outcome so the team can see what still needs attention.</li></ol></div></section>
